2026-09-27T10:19:16.1576317Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1576479Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1576717Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1576937Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1577009Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1577180Z ================
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1577280Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1577516Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1577806Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1577975Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1578069Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1578286Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1578425Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1578533Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1578889Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1579175Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1579721Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1580138Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1580225Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1580565Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1581642Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1581873Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1582116Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1582431Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1582501Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1582657Z ========
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1582748Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1583762Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1584641Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1584758Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1585000Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1640568Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1641168Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1641721Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1642153Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1642537Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1642621Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1642820Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1642935Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1643787Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1644711Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1645245Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1645962Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:19:16.1646133Z 
